			"notes": {
				"rationale": "gehen is the finite VERB and spazieren its infinitive, a VERB of its own; abends between them is free. spazieren gehen has a Duden headword but means what its words say, 'go walking', like einkaufen gehen, so it fails de/idiom, and a verb + verb unit needs both (#723). This replaces the Imported Case's one VERB over [gehen, spazieren] (#82's policy). Ruled by the user on #739 (2026-10-01), reversing #743 SZ-B7."
			},
